>> come back up. Or use teleport control and go straight there.
> 
> Heh heh, that's a joke, isn't it?

Not really. Sometimes if you're having problems going down it can be as 
easy to work your way up instead, and remember, if you visit a level when 
you're a low XL then you don't get as nasty a set of monsters. So if you 
were to dig straight down early and then teleport back up you'd find all 
the levels you had visited on the way down are comparatively easy when you 
come to do them properly.

> 
> Would you mind explaining the clairvoyance thing? How does that tie in
> with gold?

Gold can buy you protection, but if you've maxed out the protection then 
you can donate smaller amounts to a priest and get clairvoyance instead. 
That means you get chunk of map filled in randomly while exploring. That's 
especially useful on maze levels but also quite good at other times.

> You mean cursed scrolls, right?

Yes.

> Also, a few things that haven't been mentioned: the PYEC and
> #twoweapon (as opposed to a shield). What do you think of them?

Never found the PYEC that exciting. #twoweapon is good for some character 
classes but it depends on your equipment: GDSM plus a shield of relection 
is a perfectly valid choice. Basically you can ascend with a wide variety 
of equipment combinations, it's not the equipment that makes the 
difference, it's the way you use it.



